Kubernetes MySQL Deployment with Persistent Storage and Secrets
This project deploys a production-ready MySQL instance on a Kubernetes cluster, utilizing explicit PersistentVolumes, PersistentVolumeClaims, Kubernetes Secrets for secure credential management, a Deployment, and a NodePort Service.

Architecture & Requirements Summary
PersistentVolume (mysql-pv):

Storage capacity of 250Mi.

Uses hostPath (/mnt/data) with ReadWriteOnce access mode and manual binding via an empty storage class (storageClassName: "").

PersistentVolumeClaim (mysql-pv-claim):

Requests 250Mi of storage and explicitly binds to mysql-pv.

Deployment (mysql-deployment):

Runs mysql:8.0 with 1 replica.

Mounts the persistent volume at /var/lib/mysql.

Service (mysql):

Exposes MySQL externally as a NodePort service on port 3307 with nodePort: 30007.

Kubernetes Secrets:

mysql-root-pass: Stores the root password (YUIidhb667).

mysql-user-pass: Stores custom user credentials (kodekloud_top / ksH85UJjhb).

mysql-db-url: Stores the initial database name (kodekloud_db4).

Environment Variables:

Injected dynamically into the MySQL container from the respective Kubernetes Secrets (MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD, MYSQL_DATABASE, MYSQL_USER, MYSQL_PASSWORD).

Deployment Manifests
The deployment is split into two sequential files to ensure proper volume binding before pod creation.

Step 1: Storage Manifest (01-storage.yaml)
YAML
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume
metadata:
  name: mysql-pv
spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 250Mi
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  storageClassName: ""
  hostPath:
    path: /mnt/data
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: mysql-pv-claim
spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  storageClassName: ""
  volumeName: mysql-pv
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 250Mi
Step 2: Application Stack Manifest (02-app.yaml)
YAML
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: mysql-root-pass
type: Opaque
stringData:
  password: YUIidhb667
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: mysql-user-pass
type: Opaque
stringData:
  username: kodekloud_top
  password: ksH85UJjhb
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: mysql-db-url
type: Opaque
stringData:
  database: kodekloud_db4
---
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: mysql-deployment
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: mysql
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: mysql
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: mysql
        image: mysql:8.0
        ports:
        - containerPort: 3306
        env:
        - name: MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: mysql-root-pass
              key: password
        - name: MYSQL_DATABASE
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: mysql-db-url
              key: database
        - name: MYSQL_USER
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: mysql-user-pass
              key: username
        - name: MYSQL_PASSWORD
          valueFrom:
            secretKeyRef:
              name: mysql-user-pass
              key: password
        volumeMounts:
        - name: mysql-storage
          mountPath: /var/lib/mysql
      volumes:
      - name: mysql-storage
        persistentVolumeClaim:
          claimName: mysql-pv-claim
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: mysql
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: mysql
  ports:
  - port: 3306
    targetPort: 3306
    nodePort: 30007
Execution Instructions
Apply the Storage Configuration:

Bash
kubectl apply -f 01-storage.yaml
Verify that both the PV and PVC status show as Bound:

Bash
kubectl get pv,pvc
Apply the Application Stack:

Bash
kubectl apply -f 02-app.yaml
Verify Deployment Health:

Bash
kubectl get all
